---
import IconHeart from '~icons/lucide/heart';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support Toolland | Toolland"
  description="Toolland is free, ad-free, and needs no sign-up. Voluntary support through Saweria helps pay for servers and new tools."
  alternates={{ id: '/dukung', en: '/en/support' }}
>
  <div class="prose-tool">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
      Support Toolland
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg">
      Toolland is free, with no ads, no sign-up, and no watermarks. If it helps your work, any
      support means a lot.
    </p>

    <div class="card my-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 border-brand-300 bg-brand-50 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900/30">
      <IconHeart class="size-8 shrink-0 text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-300" aria-hidden="true" />
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Donate through Saweria</p>
        <p class="text-sm">
          Pay with QRIS, e-wallets, or bank transfer. Any amount, no account needed.
        </p>
      </div>
      {SITE.saweria ? (
        <a href={SITE.saweria} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary no-underline">
          Support on Saweria
        </a>
      ) : (
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold">The donation page is being set up.</p>
      )}
    </div>

    <h2>What your support pays for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Server and domain costs.</strong> Most tools run in your browser, but the website
        still needs a server, a domain, and bandwidth to deliver WebAssembly codecs and AI models to
        every visitor.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server-side tools.</strong> Word, Excel, and PowerPoint to PDF, PDF to Word, ODT to
        DOCX, and maximum PDF compression run on our own server without storing files.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Time to build new tools</strong> and keep everything fast.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Other ways to help</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Share Toolland with friends, classmates, or colleagues.</li>
      <li>
        Report bugs or suggest new tools on <a href={`${SITE.repo}/issues`}>GitHub</a>. Toolland is
        open source (AGPL-3.0).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Donations are voluntary. Every tool stays free, with or without a donation.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
